{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PREMISE CORRECTION (root-cause investigation, AC1).\n\nThe reported behaviour is NOT inconsistent — advisory finding text is published NOWHERE, on EVERY change. Change 1636 is not a counter-example.\n\nLive Gerrit API evidence (RebarBotNava, /a/changes/<n>/...):\n- GET revisions/current/comments -> {} (empty) for 1636, 1666 AND 1685. No inline comments on any of them, including the supposed counter-example.\n- GET revisions/current/robotcomments -> plain-text body 'robot comments unsupported' for all three. This Gerrit server has robot comments DISABLED/REMOVED, so the bot's robot-comment payload is a dead surface here.\n- The rebar-review-bot change message on all three is identical in shape, e.g. 1636 'Patch Set 1: LLM-Review+1 / [LLM-Review: PASS] / rebar code review passed. 2 advisory finding(s) (non-blocking).' — 1666 PS1 says '4 advisory finding(s)', 1685 PS1 says '2 advisory finding(s)'. Count only, in all three cases.\n\nSo the earlier '1636 got inline comments' observation was mistaken (most likely rebar review-code local CLI output was read as Gerrit state).\n\nROOT CAUSE (single, deterministic — not an anchoring or auth failure):\nsrc/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py:132 _summarize(), PASS branch, lines 134-138 renders only len(verdict['advisory']) as a count and never itemises the findings. The 'finding' branch (lines 139-152) itemises BLOCKING findings only — advisory text is dropped there too. _translate_findings (adapter.py:114) additionally discards each finding's 'location' field, so no anchor ever reaches the Gerrit layer. voter.py:700 calls gc.post_vote(change_id, revision, value, message) with four positional args, so gerrit_client.post_vote's robot_comments parameter (gerrit_client.py:277-294) is never supplied by production code and always falls back to the single /PATCHSET_LEVEL robot comment carrying the same message string. No code path anywhere constructs a per-file/per-line comment map.\n\nTherefore: hypothesis 'anchor-less findings silently dropped' = partially right (locations ARE discarded, at adapter.py:114) but the mechanism is broader — advisory findings are never rendered at all, anchored or not. Hypotheses 'posting call fails/auth' and 'size threshold' are REJECTED: the vote POST succeeds (LLM-Review+1 landed on all three) and the count is unbounded.\n\nSecondary finding worth carrying into the fix: because robot comments are unsupported on this server, the review message body is the ONLY surface proven to render, so the fix must guarantee body enumeration and treat inline comments as an additive bonus."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786574667019496001,"uuid":"670445cb-7c52-499b-85a4-26eaaead0630"}